## Selected quality framework

Read the [quality guide](quality-guide.md), [quality policy](quality-policy.md),
[project profile](quality-profile.json) and [profile schema](quality-profile.schema.json).
The copied catalog is managed reference material. The profile and four files in
`docs/quality/` are project-owned and preserved during ordinary updates.

Complete and independently review the inactive seed before a separate activation
PR. No application check, coverage threshold, reviewed commit or certification is
invented by installation. Run
`python .engineering-backbone/quality-guard.py validate --root .` from the repository
root to check structure only; the pinned governance workflow uses its own reviewed guard/catalog instead
of candidate-owned tooling. Updated managed catalog/guidance needs reviewed manual
integration and a matching immutable workflow pin. Refresh preserved native
instructions through that reviewed migration where necessary.

Read the [navigation guide](navigation-guide.md) and complete the inactive
[dependency contract](dependencies.json) against its [schema](dependencies.schema.json)
and project-owned [compatibility document](../docs/dependency-compatibility.md).
Its real manifest, resolution/runtime and Dockerfile paths must be covered by the
matching navigation component. Adopt active quality/workflows/navigation first;
then review the complete inactive dependency seed before enabled-only activation.
Copier preserves the project contract/document and existing application Dockerfiles.
It supplies no inferred package versions or application container. Use matching
reviewed guard/workflow pins, actual checks and refreshed native instructions.
